The paper’s native witness is not an edge set but a collection of cluster-respecting injective vertex maps, with cross-graph edge-disjointness. Its proof is explicitly algorithmic in spirit—partitioning clusters, then repeatedly finding pseudorandom hypergraph matchings—so I’m checking whether a finite benchmark derived from those exact objects has a meaningful compact insight, rather than merely turning the theorem into an ordinary graph search.
