/tmp/tmp.1TfCAgTpt3/approximate_decomp_blow_up.tex:1732:Hence, there exists a subgraph $Z^H_i\subseteq Z^H_i(\phi^\ast)$ that satisfies~\ref{exc sr}, \ref{exc triple} and~\ref{exc testers}, which can be seen by keeping each edge in $Z^H_i(\phi^\ast)[X^H_i\sm\tX^H_i,V_i]$ independently at random with probability $\alpha_Z$ and by possibly removing some edges incident to $x_i\in\tX_i^H$ in  $Z^H_i(\phi^\ast)$ deterministically.\COMMENT{Use McDiarmid's inequality to obtain concentration for~\ref{exc testers}.}
/tmp/tmp.1TfCAgTpt3/approximate_decomp_blow_up.tex:1744:We inductively prove that the following statement~\ind{t} holds for all $t\in[r]_0$, which will provide a partial packing of $\cH$ into $G_A$. 
