+The paper's Section 4.1 defines a conflict-free packing as a collection of
+injective vertex maps whose image edges do not overlap.  This module asks for
+exactly such a witness in the simpler two-cluster setting of Theorem 1.1: two
+labelled perfect matchings must be packed edge-disjointly into one bipartite
+host graph.  Instances are inverse-generated from cyclic edge orbits and then
