- Near-decomposition certificates contain `Θ(n²)` vertex images, exceeding the 256-atom limit before the paper’s asymptotic regime applies.
- A maximal writable perfect-matching specialization was solved by repeated Hopcroft–Karp on 100/100 instances in a median 10,654.5 probes and 0.006336 seconds. Its compact route is the same computation.

Accordingly, no generator, self-test, README, or oracle transcripts were created, as required for a decisive Step-0 rejection. See the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2001.03506v1) and the [algorithmic treatment of its pseudorandom-matching ingredient](https://ieee-focs.org/FOCS-2021-Papers/pdfs/FOCS2021-5stbVHiOp5jRHWlSl41FkR/205500b080/205500b080.pdf).
