The source confirms the critical distinctions: Section 1.1 asks for a packing map, not necessarily full edge coverage; Theorem 1.1 is an asymptotic existence theorem in a dense super-regular slack regime; and Sections 3–5 produce the packing through pseudorandom hypergraph matchings plus blow-up-lemma completion. That rules out an honest Track A claim for the theorem-promised distribution. I’m now auditing whether the existing cyclic specialization is a legitimate Track B compression or an added puzzle that no longer represents the paper.
