codex
A broader escalation audit found a subtle issue the required eight seeds would miss: the 64-restart greedy attack begins succeeding occasionally once host degree reaches 12 (1/300 at degree 12, rising thereafter). I’m capping fixed-length escalation at degree 11, where it was 0/300, rather than hiding that tail behind the mandated 0/8 panel. Beyond that, increasing `n` would exceed the answer-atom cap.
