codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s native graph-packing definition ([full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2001.03506)).

Key results:

- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000; analytic upper bound \(2.29\times10^{-33}\).
- Four no-tool attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference augmenting-path algorithm: 8/8, averaging 10,290 edge probes.
- Shipping answer:  reti 230 bisclak elements, 611 characters, conservative 481 tokens.
- Intended reciprocal-coordinate route: 252 operations.
- Canonical-key tests: 40/40 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

Files:

- [gen_2001_03506.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/gen_2001_03506.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/llm craz_loop_transcriptnym.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2001.03506/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only incomplete requirement is external oracle validation: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo request before inference. The transcripts preserve those service errors; they are not claimed as model failures. The family should not be treated as shippable until the three harness runs are repeated with a funded key.
